THOUGHT: The syntax error comes from a duplicated method signature line. I need to clean this up so there is a single, correctly annotated override of createMock that delegates to doCreateMock, asserts non-null via Objects.requireNonNull, and keeps doCreateMock nullable for spy usage. Then I’ll re-run the build to confirm the NullAway error is resolved and no new ones are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/mockito && sed -i '299,304c\  @Override
  public <T> T createMock(MockCreationSettings<T> settings, MockHandler handler) {
    T instance = doCreateMock(settings, handler, false);
    return java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(
        instance, "InlineByteBuddyMockMaker.createMock must not return null");
  }' src/main/java/org/mockito/internal/creation/bytebuddy/InlineByteBuddyMockMaker.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

